# Claude Code OAuth token — get one by running `claude setup-token` on your host.
# Lets the agent use your Claude subscription instead of an API key.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# Or use an Anthropic API key instead — uncomment and fill in:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GitHub token for the sandbox — the agent uses it only to read and comment on issues.
# Use an issues-only token, never one that can push: the agents read issue text anyone
# can write. Create a fine-grained token: https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
# Repository access: this repository only. Permissions: Issues (Read and write), Metadata (Read).
# Left blank, the sandbox gets no GitHub token; your shell's GH_TOKEN is never passed in.
SANDBOX_GH_TOKEN=
